WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:04.300
-Ronnie, welcome to the show.
I'm so happy to --

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.667
We hung out maybe a month ago
in London

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.234
and we had
the greatest time ever.

00:00:08.234 --> 00:00:10.567
You were so funny.
You're the life of the party.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:14.334
-So is he. He's like this
all day long, you know.

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:16.567
-Am I too high-energy?
-I went for dinner with him,

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.534
and I had to have
a lay-down first.

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:21.734
-Yeah. This is actually true.
We did the interview.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.067
-Yeah.
-Global interview.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.033
We were talking about
"Hackney Diamonds,"

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:26.901
which is finally out
this Friday.

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:29.734
And we get to dinner,
and you're not there,

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:32.200
and we go,
"Where's Ronnie and Sally?"

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.434
And your wife sent a picture.

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:35.767
She goes,
"Yeah, Ronnie's taking a nap."

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:37.701
And there's you taking a nap.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:41.400
-I had to in order to
stay up all night with him.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.667
But, yeah,
that's a Rolling Stone blanket

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:47.200
made of T-shirts
that otherwise would get lost.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.734
I think it was a great idea.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.567
-It's kind of a brilliant idea.
These are all Rolling Stones --

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:52.901
I go, "Do you sleep
with your swag?"

00:00:52.901 --> 00:00:55.167
And you were like, "No.
I get all these T-shirts

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:56.868
and all this stuff and I go,
'What to do with it?'"

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:58.634
So you made it into a quilt.

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:02.067
-Yeah, well, it's, like,
lamb's wool-lined T-shirts.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:04.834
And it's, like, so warm.

00:01:04.834 --> 00:01:06.734
-It's super comfy. I love it.

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:08.601
Let's talk about the album.
Here we go.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:11.200
It's been almost 20 years
since --

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.567
-It's the first time
I seen one opened up.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:15.067
-Is that right?
-...shrink wrap.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:17.434
Wow!
-I'm honored!

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:20.300
-Hey, everybody!

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.200
Welcome to the album.
I'm really honored.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.968
-How does it -- How does it feel

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:27.601
to have a new
Rolling Stones album?

00:01:27.601 --> 00:01:29.634
-Well, I can say
it's about time.

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:31.000
-Yes. Of course.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.133
20 years is just about
the right amount of time.

00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:34.801
-It feels so exciting

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:36.400
because I'm excited

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.634
about every track on it.
-Yes.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:42.901
-Every track has got
a different thing to say

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:44.601
and a different direction.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.067
-I mean, we can talk
about things now.

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.868
We weren't even allowed
to talk about everything.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:50.400
You do a great song
with Lady Gaga,

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.868
"Sweet Sounds of Heaven,"
that is unbelievable.

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.634
And Stevie Wonder.
-Yes.

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:57.767
-And Elton John and --
-Yeah, but Stevie Wonder

00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:01.734
and Lady are on
"Sweet Sound of Heaven,"

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:06.667
which you may have already
heard because the only ones --

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.501
only tracks
to be released so far

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:12.367
are "Angry"
and "Sweet Sound of Heaven."

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:14.400
And I'm just blown away
with them.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.868
I mean, to be in the studio
with that genius Stevie Wonder.

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:20.501
-Yes, but which one are you
looking forward to the audience

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:22.667
hearing, like,
that aren't those two?

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:25.434
Is it the --
-"Whole Wide World."

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:28.267
-Yeah, that's a great --
-It's a great up-tempo...

00:02:28.267 --> 00:02:30.033
♪ Da da da da da da da da ♪

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:32.667
-Yes. Yeah. I love it. Yeah.
Yeah. Okay. Good. That's good.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.901
-You're gonna love that.
-You're gonna love that one.

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:37.734
-And for the other side
of the coin,

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:40.701
there's a country kind of
flavored song

00:02:40.701 --> 00:02:43.033
called "Dreamy Skies"

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:45.267
where I get to play
a little slide and mix things.

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:46.968
It's very country.
-I should mention, also,

00:02:46.968 --> 00:02:51.167
this was made after
the passing of Charlie Watts,

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:54.601
who is obviously your brother
and your band member,

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:55.834
one of the greatest drummers.

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:58.400
-Yeah, well, some things
are beyond our control,

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.267
and losing Charlie
was one of those things.

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:05.868
But before he did pass,
he said to me and to the band --

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:08.868
Because I was the last one
to see him in his hospital room.

00:03:08.868 --> 00:03:11.234
And he said, "Just make sure

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:15.234
that you get Steve Jordan
to cover for me.

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:18.601
And when I get well,
I can come, you know."

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:19.834
But he said, "Until then,

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:22.200
please make sure
you have Steve Jordan."

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:26.033
And Steve is like a rocket ship
behind you. It's so fantastic.

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:27.934
-And so you got Steve.
-You know Steve.

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.868
-Yeah. Absolutely. Yeah.
We love Steve. That's wild.

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:31.701
But you got to do two songs --

00:03:31.701 --> 00:03:33.667
Charlie plays on two songs
on this album.

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:35.701
-Yeah.
And Andrew Watt, our producer,

00:03:35.701 --> 00:03:37.601
a magic producer.
-Andrew Watt, by the way --

00:03:37.601 --> 00:03:40.434
-Pulled this out of the hat.
-What a great job he did.

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:42.434
-Yeah, well, he did.

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:44.701
He had some wonderful
little ideas, like,

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:49.334
"Okay, let's use the drum track
of Charlie

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:51.133
on 'Live by the Sword,'

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:55.868
and I'll call in Bill Wyman
to get the bass."

00:03:55.868 --> 00:04:01.000
And so in Charlie's absence,
we got the band --

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.601
the original band back together.

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:04.200
-Original Rolling Stones. Yeah.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.467
When you came
onto the Rolling Stones,

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:08.100
that was '75, '76?

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.167
-Yeah. It was '74. My first solo
album with "Shirley."

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:14.934
-Oh, yeah.
You do know the song! A-ha!

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:16.434
Yeah, you're just
playing with me. Yeah.

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:18.033
-In fact, it didn't sound
anything like it.

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:20.100
That's the funk version.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.534
-That's the fun part.
That's what makes it fun.

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:25.634
But, so,
you come into the Stones.

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:27.334
They're already
the Rolling Stones.

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:28.801
Did you -- Were you a fan
of the band? Did you --

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.534
-Yeah.
Ever since I was at college.

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.501
-Yeah.
-I used to race home to see them

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:34.868
on this show called
"Ready Steady Go!"

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:36.567
and "Thank Your Lucky Stars."

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:39.367
All the English TV shows we had.

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:42.534
And I'd say,
"That's my kind of music.

00:04:42.534 --> 00:04:44.100
I'm going to be in that band!"

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.634
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:47.901
-And they called you and said,
"Do you want to join the band?"

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:49.300
And you're like,
"Yeah, of course."

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.000
-Yeah, but a series
of wonderful coincidences

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.100
being in the right place
at the right time

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.634
made it happen for me.

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.901
You know, it was just --
-Was it Keith --

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:59.067
Was it Keith
who you were friends with?

00:04:59.067 --> 00:05:00.868
There's a picture
of you and Keith, by the way,

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:02.901
This is 1979, I believe.

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:04.801
But was it Keith who --

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:07.133
I mean, what else could you be
besides rock stars

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:08.868
in this photo?

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:10.634
I mean, come on.
This is just legendary.

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:12.400
-And that's on board our plane,
as well.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:15.834
-Yes. Of course it is.
Why not? Yeah, exactly.

00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:18.634
So you get together, you play
with the Rolling Stones.

00:05:18.634 --> 00:05:22.133
You're just legendary.
What a great career.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:25.367
And then this album comes out
and kind of --

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:27.434
Can we talk about this song?

00:05:27.434 --> 00:05:29.300
-"Bite My Head Off."
-"Bite My Head Off."

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.667
-That's wonderful. We just
rehearsed that yesterday.

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:35.400
We've been doing a little bit
of rehearsing to see

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:40.200
how these songs translate live,
and they're really cooking.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.267
-Can you tell people who is
a special guest on that song?

00:05:42.267 --> 00:05:45.400
-Paul McCartney --
his big dream -- said...

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:50.100
-A Beatle is on
the Rolling Stones album!

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:52.868
A Beatle is on
the Rolling Stones album!

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:55.901
What is going on?!

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:57.501
-Yeah. Well, the song goes...

00:05:57.501 --> 00:06:00.267
♪ Bah bah bah bah bah bah bah
bah bah bah dah dah dah dah ♪

00:06:00.267 --> 00:06:02.067
♪ Bite my head off ♪
Right?

00:06:02.067 --> 00:06:06.067
And Paul --
he was so blown away.

00:06:06.067 --> 00:06:08.934
He was a bit like a schoolboy,
you know?

00:06:08.934 --> 00:06:12.033
A kid in a toy shop, you know?
-Yeah.

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:14.634
-And he loved it.
He said, "My dream!"

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:16.234
-Really?

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:19.200
-He said, "A Beatle gets to play
on a Rolling Stones album!"

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.300
Yeah, he was really knocked out.
Yeah.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.367
-It's so good.
Wait till you hear this album.

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:26.234
It's getting great reviews,
so congratulations on that.

00:06:26.234 --> 00:06:28.434
-Yeah.
I also want to mention,

00:06:28.434 --> 00:06:30.667
by the way, that -- I know
everyone probably knows this,

00:06:30.667 --> 00:06:33.901
but maybe if you don't,
you're an amazing painter.

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:35.567
You really are a great artist.

00:06:35.567 --> 00:06:36.834
-Thanks. I've been painting
since I was little.

00:06:36.834 --> 00:06:39.734
-Yeah. Was your family into --

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:42.567
-Yeah, my two older brothers.

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:45.133
I grew up eight years
behind Ted,

00:06:45.133 --> 00:06:48.434
ten years behind Art.
-Great name.

00:06:48.434 --> 00:06:52.133
-And all of our initials
spell ART -- Art, Ron, and Ted.

00:06:52.133 --> 00:06:53.968
Anyway, so the thing is...
-Wow.

00:06:53.968 --> 00:06:55.934
-If they --
They were musicians, too.

00:06:55.934 --> 00:06:57.534
So if they played, I would play.

00:06:57.534 --> 00:07:00.200
And if they painted,
I would paint.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.534
And it just stuck with me
all the years.

00:07:02.534 --> 00:07:04.734
-I figured I'd show
just a couple just to see...

00:07:04.734 --> 00:07:08.567
-I just copied that.
That's a tribute to Van Gogh.

00:07:08.567 --> 00:07:10.667
-Yeah. It's fantastic.

00:07:10.667 --> 00:07:14.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:14.334 --> 00:07:16.834
-And this is a tribute
to Delacroix,

00:07:16.834 --> 00:07:19.133
one of my favorite
French painters.

00:07:19.133 --> 00:07:20.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:20.634 --> 00:07:25.601
-This is -- You're so talented.
I can't -- And this one...

00:07:25.601 --> 00:07:28.100
-This is a little tribute
to "Angry."

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.701
-Yeah.

00:07:29.701 --> 00:07:32.400
-It's called
"Barcelona Diamonds."

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.968
-Yeah. Barcelona.

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:38.400
Go to RonnieWood.com and
check out more of Ronnie's art.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:40.701
I'm just so happy
that I know you,

00:07:40.701 --> 00:07:42.634
and I'm happy that you came on.

00:07:42.634 --> 00:07:44.100
I know you don't really do
talk shows.

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.534
This means so much to me.

00:07:45.534 --> 00:07:47.133
And to meet your family
all backstage.

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:50.267
The most beautiful family.
And your daughters are gorgeous.

00:07:50.267 --> 00:07:52.167
And I just want to say
thank you so much

00:07:52.167 --> 00:07:53.634
and congrats on the record.

00:07:53.634 --> 00:07:55.801
-You were so nice to them.
You made them feel so warm.

00:07:55.801 --> 00:07:58.434
-The best. This is Ronnie Wood,
ladies and gentlemen!

00:07:58.434 --> 00:08:00.534
"Hackney Diamonds"
is out this Friday.

00:08:00.534 --> 00:08:02.000
-Thank you!
-This Friday!

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.968
We'll be right back
with Sam Heughan.

00:08:03.968 --> 00:08:05.467
Stick around, everybody!

